00:06:51,840 --> 00:07:07,876
And what we do here is, we allow simply for the time t basin of attraction of the safe set, which is the set of states in the state space, which are guaranteed to converge to the safe set when the backup control input is applied.

49
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:14,980
We're going to assume that this basin of attraction does not intersect the safe set for some known backup time.

50
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:30,244
And the reason why this is important is because the fact that SB is robustly forward invariant under the backup control policy implies that this time T basin of attraction is also robustly forward invariant as well, regardless of your choice of the backup time.

51
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:37,444
and what we're going to do in the following is we're going to allow the system to move within the time t basin of attraction of the system.

