Okay, so due to time constraints on the presentation, I don't have time to really get into the full nuance and gravity of our results, but I'm presenting here an algorithm for runtime assurance for non-deterministic systems.

55
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:12,228
so what's going on here is that at every time step, this algorithm will predict a reachable set using the mixed monotonicity tools in the embedding system by simulating a trajectory forward.

56
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:20,720
and then we're going to ensure that a barrier condition is satisfied at the corners of the rectangular reachable set approximation derived.

